Why this is a separate file
---------------------------

LICENSE is the verbatim GPL-2.0 text. The only

    Copyright (C) <year>  <name of author>

line in it belongs to the licence's own "How to Apply These Terms to Your New
Programs" appendix. That is an example intended to be copied into your own
files -- not a blank to be filled in inside the licence. Editing it would
modify the licence text itself, which is not something a licensee should do.

GPL-2.0 section 1 asks for an appropriate copyright notice on each copy, and
the licence's "How to Apply These Terms" appendix recommends putting one at the
start of each source file. Per-file headers were deliberately not used here:
when this was decided, the fork tracked an active upstream, and a header added
to every file would have conflicted with essentially any upstream change. The
same reasoning kept stylistic lint rules off (see ruff.toml) and kept every
pre-commit hook read-only. Upstream has been inactive since 2026-07-19 and this
fork is paused; whoever resumes it should revisit this, and #11 with it.

A single file naming the holder of this fork's changes is the version of that
notice which survives an upstream sync.

See issue #7.
